an optimizing brainfuck compiler for Linux AMD64, (and cross-platform interpreter)

there is a compiler located at compiler/
It is very fast,
I have also made a (somewhat) "simple" method of optimizing specific algorithms,
you just make a function that can detect it, write your own assembly for it,
and call it from the optimize_brainfuck() function in the brainfuck.c source
file

and there is an interpreter located at interpreter/

to build the interpreter, you don't need instructions, its literally 1 file

to build the compiler, first cd into the compiler/ directory,
then run `make all` and add -j$(nproc) if you wish

that's all!

brainfuck examples:
https://copy.sh/brainfuck

